        "original_id": "34cad90f-becb-508c-9609-bfe2e99612a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: The Periodic Table of Videos, Periodic Videos, Numberphile\n- People: Brady Haran, Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang\n- Organizations: BBC News, University of Nottingham, YouTube\n- Roles: video journalist, independent filmmaker\n- Topics: chemical elements, the periodic table\n\nFacts:\n- Brady John Haran was born on 18 June 1976.\n- Brady Haran is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist.\n- Brady Haran is known for educational videos and documentary films produced for BBC News.\n- Brady Haran is also known for his YouTube channels Periodic Videos and Numberphile.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is published on YouTube.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is produced by Brady Haran, a former BBC video journalist.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos features Sir Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, and others at the University of Nottingham.\n- Sir Martyn Poliakoff is identified in the series as \"The Professor\".",
